# Normalize line endings: text files store LF in the repo, checked out native.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets (future /ue project) — never normalize/diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.uasset binary
*.umap   binary
*.fbx    binary
*.wav    binary
*.ogg    binary
*.uasset filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.umap filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text   # RETIRED 2026-08-03, see the note below
# *.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text   # RETIRED 2026-08-03, see the note below
# The two explicit path rules the retirement note below asks for (BT-60). The
# blanket retirement also removed the SMUDGE filter from the .png files that
# were ALREADY in LFS, so a fresh clone wrote 130-byte pointer TEXT into
# assets/textures/dist/*.png and into the one LFS probe fixture. Those are
# genuinely large binaries, they are still LFS objects in history, and without
# these rules every clone silently ships the app 25 unreadable textures.
assets/textures/dist/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
web/tools/smoke/fixtures/RN958_ripple_frames.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.zip filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.exr filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY *.png AND *.jpg LEFT LFS, 2026-08-03.
#
# These rules were written for the Unreal attempt, where .png meant a source
# texture. They also caught every screenshot a lane produces as evidence, and
# lanes produce dozens a session: 1,169 screenshots had reached 941 MB, against
# GitHub's 1 GB free LFS allowance, and 773 MB of that arrived in one fortnight.
#
# Existing screenshots stay as LFS pointers (813 MB, inside the allowance).
# New ones are ordinary git blobs, so the LFS bill stops growing.
#
# If you are adding a genuinely large binary, add an explicit rule for it by
# path rather than reinstating a blanket extension rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
